WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.141
This ink costs more than champagne.

00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:04.112
In a 2022 Which?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.865
example, one Epson ink cost one pound

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:08.478
78 a millilitre.

00:00:08.488 --> 00:00:12.016
Dom Perignon champagne came to 24 pence.

00:00:12.026 --> 00:00:14.614
The ink was over seven times dearer.

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:16.630
And cheaper third-party inks?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.402
Which?

00:00:17.452 --> 00:00:19.293
found the best came very close in

00:00:19.303 --> 00:00:20.405
print quality.

00:00:20.415 --> 00:00:23.592
Some HP printers even
refuse cartridges with

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:25.144
non-HP chips.

00:00:25.154 --> 00:00:26.819
So why is the printer itself so

00:00:26.829 --> 00:00:27.517
cheap?

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.685
It's the bait.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.285
Makers sell printers cheap, sometimes at a

00:00:31.295 --> 00:00:33.433
loss, and earn it back on ink.
